{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Who found the mules.</b> Rashi interpreted: he introduced unfit creatures into the world. And if you ask: earlier, in the portion of Toledot, at ״״כי גדל מאד״״, Rashi interpreted that they would say ״״manure of his mules״״ etc. — if so, it implies they already existed. Rather, this is what it says: <b>found the mules</b> — he was the first to mate a jenny with a stallion, but previously there were no mules, neither through the animals themselves nor through others. The expression מצא means: he first discovered this wisdom — that when two species interbreed, a different species emerges, such as a mule from a horse and a donkey. For any mule whose ears are fine, its mother was a mare and its father a donkey; and any whose ears are coarse, its mother was a jenny and its father a stallion. And since the spirit of HaShem does not find favor with this practice, there is no creature that issues from two species that can reproduce. Another interpretation: creatures that come from these two species were not included in the blessing ״״פרו ורבו״״ when they emerged from the Ark; therefore they neither give birth nor impregnate."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:37.019630169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}